{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q3266534","formula":"C₆H₁₂O₅","hill":"C6H12O5","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":6.0,"H":12.0,"O":5.0},"names":{"en":"2-deoxy-D-glucose"},"descriptions":{"en":"2-Deoxy-d-glucose is a glucose molecule which has the 2-hydroxyl group replaced by hydrogen, so that it cannot undergo further glycolysis. As such; it acts to competitively inhibit the production of glucose-6-phosphate from glucose at the phosphoglucoisomerase level (step 2 of glycolysis). 2-Deoxyglucose labeled with tritium or carbon-14 has been a popular ligand for laboratory research in animal models, where distribution is assessed by tissue-slicing followed by autoradiography, sometimes in tandem with either conventional or electron microscopy."},"fame":14,"pubchemCid":108223,"mass":164.16,"charge":0,"smiles":"C(C=O)[C@H]([C@@H]([C@@H](CO)O)O)O","inchikey":"VRYALKFFQXWPIH-PBXRRBTRSA-N","iupac":"(3R,4S,5R)-3,4,5,6-tetrahydroxyhexanal","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"108223","atoms":23,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.423,"y":1.484,"z":0.674,"el":"O"},{"x":1.093,"y":-0.813,"z":1.121,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.985,"y":-1.64,"z":-0.475,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.401,"y":0.754,"z":-0.795,"el":"O"},{"x":4.159,"y":0.184,"z":0.174,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.588,"y":0.329,"z":-0.159,"el":"C"},{"x":0.781,"y":-0.373,"z":-0.208,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.746,"y":-0.525,"z":0.387,"el":"C"},{"x":1.924,"y":0.534,"z":-0.661,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.056,"y":0.256,"z":0.494,"el":"C"},{"x":3.243,"y":-0.19,"z":-0.551,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.823,"y":0.679,"z":-1.171,"el":"H"},{"x":0.729,"y":-1.266,"z":-0.841,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.496,"y":-0.912,"z":1.381,"el":"H"},{"x":1.786,"y":0.849,"z":-1.7,"el":"H"},{"x":1.998,"y":1.431,"z":-0.036,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.971,"y":1.102,"z":1.182,"el":"H"},{"x":-3.875,"y":-0.387,"z":0.832,"e